  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "tl;dr: Make sure it also posts the same content as the Official X Account (@VRChat), like updates, dev update summaries, server statuses, and chit-chats.\n\nRecently, the JP official account seems to be increasingly focused on amplifying posts from partner companies, while other posts mostly focus on VRC+.\n\nI fully understand that partnerships with companies are essential and that increasing the number of VRC+ users is important for the current VRChat.\n\nHowever, when the account primarily consists of such posts, it becomes less useful for community users.\n\nWhen the account was first launched, it shared summaries of developer updates and off-topic posts, which I found both interesting and very helpful. Since 2024, however, those types of posts have largely disappeared, and the account has mainly been used to amplify partner content and provide follow-up posts, which has made it feel less useful than before.\n\nMany of us would like to receive official information in our own language. Currently, some community members translate and share official English announcements, and other users rely on those translations to stay up to date.\n\nThe JP official account has significant influence and importance when it comes to information dissemination, and I believe the team managing it is well aware of this. I also believe that many users are hoping for this kind of posting, like from official accounts (@VRChat).\n\nI want to ask VRChat to reconsider the current management policy of the JP official account and help make it a more useful resource for the JP community.",
